{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>לֹא תִהְיֶה אֵשֶׁת הַמֵּת</b> — a warning to her and to one who lies with her; she and the one who lies with her are liable to lashes. And the verse's saying <b>יְבָמָהּ יָבֹא עָלֶיהָ</b> alludes that there is no obligation upon the levir except a single act of intercourse, as in the statement of Rabbi Yosei (Shabbat 118b): חָמֵשׁ בְּעִילוֹת בָּעַלְתִּי וְחָמֵשׁ נְטִיעוֹת נָטַעְתִּי, and they said in the Jerusalem Talmud (Yevamot 1:1) that five yevamot fell to him from five brothers and he performed yibum once for each one. And the verse's saying <b>וּלְקָחָהּ</b> — lest you say that she is forbidden to him from this point onward; Scripture therefore says ״וּלְקָחָהּ לוֹ לְאִשָּׁה״ — the permission is in his hand whether he wishes to maintain her permanently. And the verse's saying <b>וְיִבְּמָהּ</b> — lest you say that none of the things stated were said except as optional, for since Scripture forbade her to the world, it permitted her to the levir, but the Torah did not obligate him in the matter — Scripture therefore says ״וְיִבְּמָהּ״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:55.590213348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}